# keep-as-module.list — symbols that MUST stay loadable modules even when
# --kernel-builtin is set ("compile most everything into the kernel"). These are the
# "except where that inhibits function" cases: out-of-tree drivers, firmware/load-order
# sensitive drivers, and things that only work when (un)loadable at runtime.
#
# One CONFIG_ symbol per line; '#' comments and blanks ignored. Add to this list when a
# built-in symbol breaks a machine. CONFIG_MODULES itself is NEVER disabled by the
# builtin sweep (out-of-tree nvidia.ko + on-demand drivers depend on module loading).
#
# Out-of-tree / proprietary (built via emerge as .ko; can't be in-tree builtin):
CONFIG_NVIDIA
CONFIG_NVIDIA_DRM
CONFIG_ZFS
CONFIG_VBOXGUEST
CONFIG_VBOXSF_FS
# nouveau MUST stay a module so the proprietary-NVIDIA images can runtime-blacklist it
# (modprobe.d). Built-in (=y) would load nouveau before the blacklist and fight nvidia.
CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU
# Firmware/load-order sensitive radios kept as modules so NetworkManager/firmware
# ordering and rfkill toggling work (built-in can race firmware availability at init):
CONFIG_IWLWIFI
CONFIG_IWLMVM
CONFIG_MT7921E
CONFIG_MT7921_COMMON
CONFIG_ATH10K
CONFIG_ATH11K
CONFIG_ATH12K
CONFIG_BRCMFMAC
CONFIG_RTW88
CONFIG_RTW89
# Bluetooth transport modules (rfkill/(un)load + firmware ordering):
CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB
# DKMS-style / commonly-rebuilt:
CONFIG_R8168
CONFIG_R8125
